{
  "node_id": "439db11e-c41b-4e4a-8358-4905dc88d009",
  "level": 0,
  "summary": "In Salve's mind a new impulse had been unexpectedly given to thoughts\nfrom which the novelty of his situation should have afforded him at\nleast a temporary relief; and he lay long awake, thinking drearily about\nElizabeth. pilot-and-his-wife\n\nby the door, looking so grand in her pride, and\nso pale with repressed mortification, and spoke so calmly, he had felt\nthat in that moment he had been separated farther from her than ever he\nhad been in all his wanderings at the other side of the globe. pilot-and-his-wife\n\nit; and now, for what I care, you may please yourself about\ncoming home, Elizabeth,\" he continued in a cold, indifferent tone.",
