  "quote_spans": [
    {
      "chunk_id": 61,
      "char_start": 567,
      "char_end": 736,
      "text": "To Elizabeth it seemed as if there was a mist\nover them all; and when Mina once asked if there was anything the matter\nwith her, she could only answer mechanically, 'No"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 64,
      "char_start": 839,
      "char_end": 1170,
      "text": "When\nhe now so unexpectedly began to press for time, at first even proposing\nto be away himself when the matter came on in his home, a feeling took\npossession of her which in her inward dread she instinctively clutched\nat as a drowning wretch at a straw, as it seemed to suggest a\npossibility even now of reconsidering her promise"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 87,
      "char_start": 1468,
      "char_end": 1792,
      "text": "When he did fall asleep at last, he dreamed that he had come\ninto a serpent's nest, and that he was engaged in a life and death\nconflict with a huge snake, that was thrusting its forked tongue at him\nfrom walls, from roof, from every side; and in the gleam of its\nvindictive eyes, he seemed all at once to recognise Paolina"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 131,
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 269,
      "text": "pilot-and-his-wife\n\nit\nwas possible that a man from the Stars and Stripes could be permitted to\ngo to church as well as other people; and on entering the building he\nhad to summon up all his self-command--he had a feeling that he was\nviolating the sanctity of the place"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 145,
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 272,
      "text": "pilot-and-his-wife\n\nby the door, looking so grand in her pride, and\nso pale with repressed mortification, and spoke so calmly, he had felt\nthat in that moment he had been separated farther from her than ever he\nhad been in all his wanderings at the other side of the globe"
    }
  ],
